body:
## Product-Owner authorization

Continuously optimize QIK-VRT by applying a dynamic simplex-style search over repository-native, evidence-bound improvement moves. The optimizer must be subordinate to existing authority/evidence/effect invariants and must never convert optimization pressure into unauthorized effects.

## Definition

The optimizer operates on an **admissible simplex of bounded repository moves** rather than treating activity as progress. At each observation it constructs a finite set of admissible candidate moves, scores them against a versioned objective vector, selects at most one causally justified move, observes the resulting state, and updates the simplex.

```text
OBSERVE
→ BIND exact head/tree/role-local state
→ ENUMERATE admissible moves
→ REJECT invariant-violating moves
→ SCORE surviving vertices
→ SELECT one bounded move or NOOP/HOLD
→ EXECUTE only within delegated repository authority
→ REOBSERVE
→ COMPARE causal delta
→ RETAIN / CONTRACT / EXPAND / REGENERATE simplex
→ RECEIPT
```

## Hard constraints

The optimizer MUST preserve:

```text
CAUSALITY != SEQUENCE
ACTIVITY != EFFECT
TRANSPORT_ACK != EFFECT_ACK
IDENTITY != EQUALITY
AUTHORITY_EFFECT != MIRROR_EFFECT
MIRROR_EFFECT != PAIR_ACKNOWLEDGEMENT
VERIFIED_IMPLEMENTATION != AUTHORITY_EFFECT
```

It MUST NOT:

- fabricate independent review authority;
- merge merely because a score improves;
- publish merely because an artifact exists;
- erase Authority/Mirror role-local identity;
- treat retries, run volume, timestamps or comment count as causal progress;
- optimize through secrets or widen credential scope;
- claim PASS, FINAL_PASS or EFFECT_ACK_DONE without observed evidence.

## Objective vector v1

Lexicographic priority, highest first:

1. eliminate deterministic correctness defects;
2. eliminate unsafe/false authority or effect inferences;
3. restore repository self-continuation/liveness without polling loops;
4. close exact-head integrity and reproducibility gaps;
5. reduce activity-without-effect / duplicate work / stale carriers;
6. reduce deterministic latency and resource waste;
7. simplify implementation while preserving semantics;
8. improve testability, observability and artifact durability;
9. identify publication-worthy, genuinely novel results.

A lower-priority gain may never compensate for a violated higher-priority invariant.

## D0 binding

Every optimization cycle terminates in the existing four-state ABI:

- `D0=0 NOOP`: no causally justified improvement remains in the bounded simplex;
- `D0=1 HOLD`: an external prerequisite or active work prevents a justified move;
- `D0=2 REOBSERVE`: the objective state is stale or a prior move requires fresh evidence;
- `D0=3 REQUEST_AUTHORITY`: the best admissible move is blocked solely by missing authority.

## Publication boundary

Publication discovery is allowed; publication completion is a separate effect lane.

An artifact becomes `PUBLICATION_WORTHY` only if it has:

- a clearly stated novel result or reusable method;
- exact repository provenance;
- reproducible tests/evidence;
- explicit formal/empirical/interpretive boundaries;
- no unresolved correctness blocker affecting the claim;
- an archival package with checksums and metadata.

Zenodo/arXiv actions require a real available publication path and observed resulting identifier/receipt. No DOI/arXiv identifier may be invented.

## Acceptance

- [ ] versioned machine-readable optimizer contract;
- [ ] stdlib-only deterministic optimizer implementation;
- [ ] negative tests for invariant violations;
- [ ] causal fingerprint excluding activity-only fields;
- [ ] bounded one-move-per-cycle behavior;
- [ ] D0 terminal classification;
- [ ] durable optimization receipts;
- [ ] publication-worthiness classifier separated from publication effect;
- [ ] canonical test-suite registration;
- [ ] Authority/Mirror role-local preservation tests;
- [ ] exact-head workflows and integrity projections;
- [ ] documentation with operational examples.

The optimizer is complete only when it can drive repository improvement without requiring the human or conversational agent to reconstruct the next deterministic step, while still stopping at genuine authority/effect boundaries.
